jprotobuf ChangeLog
===================

Version 1.1.1 (2026-10-09)
--------------------------

Fixes and performance work; no API changes. Parsing is slightly stricter and
the writer's encoding of very large field numbers and `sint32` values is now
canonical (see below).

### Fixed

- Reject length-delimited fields whose declared length does not fit a signed
  32-bit int, and tags wider than 32 bits. Both were truncated to `int` before
  being checked, so a length of 2^32 + 3 was read as 3, 2^32 as 0, and a tag of
  2^32 + 8 as field 1, letting this parser read different fields from the same
  bytes than a strict one. They now throw `ProtobufParseException`; a negative
  length is reported with its full 64-bit value. (Security: parser
  differential.)
- `ProtobufWriter` wrote field numbers of 2^28 and above, and `sint32` values
  of magnitude 2^30 or more, as 10-byte varints because the `int` was
  sign-extended; they are now the canonical 5 bytes. The previous output still
  decoded to the same values.
- `ByteBufferChannel` no longer hangs forever when growing past 1 GiB (the
  capacity doubled through `Integer.MIN_VALUE` to zero), or when created with
  zero capacity. Growth is capped at `Integer.MAX_VALUE - 8` and a write that
  would need more throws `IOException`.
- `ProtobufWriter` no longer spins forever when the channel's `write` returns
  a negative value; it throws `ClosedChannelException`.

### Performance

- Parser: finishing a field is O(1) regardless of nesting depth (message ends
  are tracked as stream offsets instead of decrementing every open level),
  roughly 4x faster on deeply nested input.
- Parser: single-byte varints (most tags and small values) take a fast path;
  multi-byte varints and short string fields parse roughly 40-70% faster.
- Writer: embedded messages reuse a scratch buffer per nesting level instead
  of allocating 64 KB each, roughly 1.8x faster on nested input and far less
  garbage.
- Writer: a tag, length and short payload go out in a single channel write,
  short ASCII strings are encoded without an intermediate `byte[]`, and
  fixed-width values are written with one put.

### Documentation

- Document the limits to set when parsing untrusted input
  (`maxLengthDelimitedSize`, `maxMessageDepth`) in the `ProtobufParser`
  Javadoc and the README, and that the buffer passed to `handleBytes` is a view
  of the input that must be copied if kept.

### Changed

- The license is now the GNU Lesser General Public License version 3 (was
  version 2.1); the full GPL v3 text it builds on is included as
  `LICENSE-GPL`.
- Test dependencies (JUnit 4, Hamcrest) are no longer kept in git; `ant test`
  downloads them from Maven Central on first use. Building and releasing the
  library downloads nothing.

Version 1.1.0 (2026-10-05)
--------------------------

### Added

- `ProtobufParser(ProtobufHandler, int maxMessageDepth, int maxLengthDelimitedSize)`
  for configurable limits on untrusted input.
- `ProtobufParser.DEFAULT_MAX_MESSAGE_DEPTH` (100) and
  `ProtobufParser.UNLIMITED_LENGTH_DELIMITED` (`Integer.MAX_VALUE`); the
  single-argument constructor keeps the previous behaviour (default depth,
  no cap on declared length-delimited sizes).

### Fixed

- Reject length-delimited fields that extend past an embedded message's
  declared length, and bound tag, varint, and fixed reads to the active
  message budget so parent parsing cannot desync on hostile wire data.

### Performance

- Parser nesting uses a fixed primitive stack instead of rebuilding per field.
- Writer coalesces tag and value into one channel write for common field types.
- Optional `ant perf` harness for ad-hoc throughput checks (not a CI gate).

Version 1.0.0 (2026-09-16)
--------------------------

Initial release (split from gumdrop).

- Zero-dependency Protocol Buffers wire-format encoder and decoder for Java
  21+.
- Push-based `ProtobufParser` with incremental `receive(ByteBuffer)` parsing,
  underflow recovery, and nested embedded-message tracking via
  `ProtobufHandler`.
- `ProtobufWriter` for varint, fixed32/64, and length-delimited fields.
- `ByteBufferChannel` as an auto-expanding in-memory `WritableByteChannel`.
- `DefaultProtobufHandler` with helpers for common scalar and bytes/string
  interpretations.
- Published API Javadoc and Maven Central coordinates (`org.bluezoo:jprotobuf`).
